# Typed symbols are keys named without their brackets, as in the Qt port:
# "<" was sent as the key "<less>", inserted as "<<less>>" (a broken
# string), and a Backspace then crashed ("bad path" in pre_correct). F12
# prints the tree (math-backspace.scm); expected:
#   (document "x<less>y" (math "a<leqslant>"))   "<" and "<" "=" in math
#   (document "x<less>y" (math "a"))             Backspace: the symbol goes
#   (document "x<less>y" (math ""))              Backspace
wait 7000
window #2
focus
click 300 400
wait 300
text x<y
key Return
text $a<=
key F12
key Backspace
wait 300
key F12
key Backspace
wait 300
key F12
wait 500
snapshot mb
